# `struct <type> [ fields ]` declares a record type, its fixed fields, and a same-named
# constructor (Data profile, spec/grammar.md#ebnf-notation's `struct-declaration ::= "struct" declared-type-name field-list`;
# spec/data-structures.md#records-and-structs, spec/data-structures.md#record-operations). Parse-only: the StructDef AST node is produced here; the constructor
# call and field access/mutation land in a later Data-profile slice.
struct point [ x y ]
